P = \frac{\binom{6}{2} \binom{4}{2} 4^2}{6^6}
\] Simplifying this expression: \[
P = \frac{\frac{6!}{2!4!} \cdot \frac{4!}{2!2!} \cdot 16}{46656} = \frac{15 \cdot 6 \cdot 16}{46656} = \frac{1440}{46656} = \frac{5}{162}
\] </think> <answer> $\frac{5}{162}$ </answer>

